pgtt for Debian
===============

Load pgtt with session_preload_libraries or LOAD.  Upstream deliberately
rejects shared_preload_libraries and PostgreSQL will not start if pgtt is put
there.

The 4.6-2PGSTY package extends the upstream 4.5.0 to 4.6.0 transition.  It
revokes PUBLIC write privileges from pgtt_schema.pg_global_temp_tables and
from every registered GTT template, while restoring PUBLIC SELECT.  Template
ownership and grants to named roles are not changed.  Roles that create,
rename, or drop global temporary tables need an explicit catalog grant such
as:

  GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE
    ON pgtt_schema.pg_global_temp_tables TO role_name;

The migration identifies templates by the registered relation name in pgtt's
fixed extension schema.  The historical relid column is deliberately ignored:
older releases stored a relfilenode there, which can be stale after rewrite or
dump/restore.  ALTER EXTENSION aborts atomically if a registered object is
missing, outside pgtt_schema, or is not an ordinary unlogged table.  Review or
remove that stale catalog row before retrying; the migration will not guess.

Databases already reporting extension version 4.6.0 cannot rerun the versioned
4.5.0-to-4.6.0 transition.  For those databases, quiesce GTT DDL and run the
package-private idempotent script with a superuser:

  major=18
  psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -d DATABASE \
    -f "/usr/share/postgresql/${major}/extension/pgtt-repair-public-acl.sql"

Set major to the installed PostgreSQL major (14 through 18).

Run the repair once in every database that has pgtt installed.  It applies the
same validation and ACL policy as the versioned migration and rolls back the
entire transaction on an unclassifiable catalog entry.
